# Compound-assign THROUGH a pointer: `*p OP= v` (Box / &-ref). Plain `*p = v`
# already lowered (lower_assign's Expr::Deref arm, Snag #26); the compound path
# had NO arm and NO catch-all, so `*b += 5` silently DROPPED the write on both
# backends (measured pre-fix: `10, 10, 99`). lower_compound_assign now has a
# Deref arm that reads the pointee THROUGH the deref place, applies the op, and
# stores back (lower-or-reject, Core #10). Same output on both C and LLVM.
#
# Core #9 lagging lane: the self-host `SCompoundAssign` lowerer handles only
# EIdentifier/EFieldAccess/EIndex and `lower_fail`s everything else, so `*p += v`
# (EDeref) is NOT yet lowered there (SH plain `*p = v` lowers; SH compound does
# not — the same asymmetry the Rust arm just closed). Lives in `known_gaps/` to
# stay OUT of the self-host runtime-diff corpus (an EXPLICIT cited lagging lane,
# not a silent CC-FAIL); the SH `EDeref` compound arm is filed with TODO:262.
# Promote to top-level when the SH compound-assign grows an EDeref arm. Wired
# C+LLVM via `run_gg` (which never invokes the self-host).

void bump(Box[int] &b, int by):
    *b += by

void main():
    Box[int] b = Box(10)
    print(*b)        # 10
    *b += 5
    print(*b)        # 15
    *b *= 2
    print(*b)        # 30
    bump(&b, 4)      # *b += 4 through a &-borrowed Box
    print(*b)        # 34
    *b = 99          # plain-= through deref (control, unchanged behavior)
    print(*b)        # 99
    print("done")
